In spite of this accident, keeping all of your potions and scrolls in a
bag is a good idea.  There are fire traps on some (perhaps all?) of the
quest levels that can explode your potions and burn your scrolls, except
the fire scroll. And even outside the quest, if you don't have
reflection, some attacks will also explode your items. I don't the think
the explosions and burning scrolls will hurt you if you have fire
resistance, but you'll still be left with fewer potions and scrolls.
Rather than keep your potions in open inventory, consider getting them
out and drinking them at a higher HP.  

Also, you might try doing the castle before the quest.  The wand of
wishing can be extremely helpful with AC by both wishing for better
armor and wishing for magic markers to write scrolls of enchant armor.
I usually do the quest fairly late, definitely after the castle and
valley.  The quest artifact is nice but not extremely important to me at
that point of the game, especially if I don't have teleport control.

